# SABOTAGE: MG-09 (ADR-049 mutation ledger; re-anchored for token binding) — `Samen.Pii.WriteGuard.plaintext_write?/2`
# is NARROWED so an in-flight plaintext whose text starts with `vt_` no longer counts as operator-authored
# PLAINTEXT. Since token binding a raw string is ALWAYS plaintext (`VaultField.cast_input/2` wraps it), so an
# operator who types a `vt_…` string into a vaulted field is authoring plaintext and must be refused.
#
# The UNDER-refusal direction: every shipped RP-L1 test writes genuine plaintext not starting with `vt_` and
# stays green under this flip. What breaks is the raw-`vt_`-string write.
#
# Flips the named MG-09 red. The anti-tautology CONTROL stays green — genuine operator
# plaintext is still refused with "no-operator-plaintext-write" — so the red fails because
# the `vt_*` arm was added, not because the guard or the vault write path broke. MG-08's
# and MG-10's reds stay green: this patch touches ONE clause.
#
# One case clause, one literal. Touches write_guard.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/pii_write_guard_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-09: an OPERATOR writing back the raw vt_* string is REFUSED
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
index 21a7b7b2..eb42de51 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
@@ -117,6 +117,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Pii.WriteGuard do
   defp plaintext_write?(changeset, name) do
     case Ash.Changeset.fetch_change(changeset, name) do
       {:ok, %Masked{}} -> false
+      {:ok, %Samen.Pii.Plaintext{value: "vt_" <> _}} -> false
       {:ok, nil} -> false
       {:ok, _plaintext} -> true
       :error -> false
